    "result_text": "The full test suite passes green (35 tests, 0 failures/errors), including the new `Cp25Tests` for email uniqueness.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule for `POST /owners` following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness rule.\n\n**New files:**\n- `RequireUniqueOwnerEmail.java` \u2014 pipeline step that reads the normalized (lower-cased) email published by `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, skips the check when email is null/blank (email is optional), and throws `OwnerEmailDuplicateException` when any existing owner's email matches case-insensitively.\n- `OwnerEmailDuplicateException.java` \u2014 checked escalation carrying the normalized email.\n- `OwnerEmailDuplicateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds **409** with `{\"errors\": [\"email\"]}`.\n- `...OwnerEmailDuplicateException.yml` \u2014 escalation handler wiring.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `uniqueEmail` step (under the `transaction` governance) right after `normalizeEmail` (so comparison happens on the lower-cased form) and before the telephone-uniqueness check.\n\nThe check compares lower-cased on both sides for defensiveness, though stored emails are already lower-cased by `NormalizeOwnerEmail`.",
